{
  "about": {
    "what": "The ship's routine: the clock, the watches, the three watch sections that keep them in turn, your own line on the watch bill, the muster at the change of your watch, and night. watch.mjs runs it.",
    "clock": "`rate` is ship seconds per real second (30: a four-hour watch is eight minutes). `start` is the day and the time a new hand comes aboard.",
    "watches": "The day's watches, in order, `from` and `to` as hh:mm. The two dog watches make seven in a day, so with three sections the watch each section keeps moves round by one every day.",
    "sections": "The watch sections. `first` is the one that keeps the middle watch on day 1; after that they take the watches in turn. `leader` is the section's leading hand, who musters it, by `id`: a person in content/people/<id>.json.",
    "you": "Your line on the bill: your `section`, your `part` of ship, where you `muster` (a room, and `at` the spot you are shown), and `shake`, the minutes before your watch you are called when you have turned in (`bunk`: the room and spot of your bunk).",
    "muster": "The muster: `early` minutes before the watch the section falls in (`hands` of them, at `line`, facing `face`; the leading hand at `leader`); at the bell the roll is called; `late` minutes after, they march `out`.",
    "night": "From `from` to `to` the passages are in red lighting (darken ship), and the hands not on watch are turned in.",
    "pipes": "What is piped and said at the change of watch, at pipe down and at call the hands. {watch} {section} {time} {muster} are filled in.",
    "drum": "Off-watch hands in the drums (hands.mjs), drawn only in the segments round you and placed only out of your sight. `max` is the most drawn at once. `uses` says, per room `use` (a key of `rooms` wins by room id), who is in a room when: the first row whose `hours` [from, to] hold the time gives `n` [fewest, most] (the count is dealt per room and half hour, so a room looks the same when you come back), their `poses` (sitChair takes the stools and chairs the sets give, else they stand) and `depts`. `ring` is the hands walking the ring corridor. `change`: from `before` minutes before a change of watch to `after` minutes after it, hands wait at the spoke lifts (`waiting` of them), and `riders` ride with you if you take a lift then. `stations`: at action stations the drum empties up the spokes: for `empty` seconds hands hurry from the rooms to the lifts and are taken up; after that only the rooms whose use is in `stay` keep anyone."
  },
